# The whole project lives in this one repository, data and all, so this file is what
# stands between 2.9 GB of working folder and a 27 MB history. Everything excluded here
# is either raw data, a download that can be fetched again or something derived that a
# notebook rebuilds on demand.

# The recordings themselves. A single one of these runs to 925 MB and GitHub refuses any
# file over 100 MB, so a push carrying them would fail outright rather than quietly
# succeed. We exclude both the folder and the extension, because a stray recording saved
# somewhere else should be caught just the same.
recordings/
*.vrs

# Model weights. Ultralytics downloads these on demand and drops them into whatever the
# working directory happens to be, so the extensions matter as much as the folder.
# The extra formats are here for when we export a model rather than just load one.
models/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.torchscript
*.safetensors

# Everything derived. The exported frames and the mp4 are rebuilt by notebook 03 from
# the recording whenever it finds them missing, so there is nothing here we would lose.
cache/
frames_*/
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov

# Meta's client SDK samples. We never edited these and extract_sdk_samples puts them
# back in one command, so they are a checkout rather than our own work.
vendor/

# The reference folder is a mixed bag, so we split it. The two papers are public and
# anyone can download them again, so 36 MB of pdf stays out. The dataset manifest beside
# them is only 104 KB and it records exactly which sequences we were looking at, so that
# one is worth versioning and it is deliberately not excluded here.
reference/*.pdf

# Where does Ultralytics put its own output ? Into a runs folder next to whatever called
# it, which for us means inside notebooks. That is a cache of annotated images rather
# than a result, so it stays out.
runs/

# Python leftovers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Jupyter keeps a shadow copy of every notebook as you work. Those are older duplicates
# of files we already track, so there is no reason to carry them.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Virtual environments never belong in here. Ours lives in the home folder instead, at
# ~/projectaria_gen2_python_env, which keeps it well clear of the repository.
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Anything holding a secret. We have no .env today and this is here so that we do not
# have to remember on the day we add one.
.env
.env.*

# macOS scatters these about. The ._ files in particular turn up whenever files get
# copied to a drive that is not formatted for the Mac. We move large files around a lot
# on this project.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd

# Word leaves a lock file beside any document it has open, named with a ~$ prefix. They
# vanish when the document is closed, so there is never a reason to commit one.
~$*

# Editor and tool settings are personal rather than part of the project.
.vscode/
.idea/

# Logs from long runs. Useful while you are watching them and not worth keeping.
*.log
